WEBVTT

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.000
Fall in!

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.970
It's the king himself...

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.830
You all have such strong, rugged features.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:20.360
I am now certain that you 
can fulfill this mission.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.700
I expect nothing but the 
best from all of you.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.410
On my very life, Your Majesty!

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.130
Well, at least...

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.720
we managed to find the wagon...

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.970
Damn it! Damn it!

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.070
Damn it!

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.950
We're only here to mess with 
you in the name of revenge.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.360
I...

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.710
I failed...

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:07.760
I failed to live up to the 
king's expectations!

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.100
How will the king punish us

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:25.340
when we report this miserable 
failure to him?

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:28.690
The two of us must resign 
ourselves... to...

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.350
H-Huh?!

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.970
The king? Not quite.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.900
The one who'll be punishing you...

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.500
is me.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.910
You're alive?!

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.800
The part about Kahvel-san 
and her two men dying

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.540
and the other two heroes falling 
in a hole was true...

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:03.470
but everything from Yotsuya-kun's 
conversion to Arteros onward was a lie!

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.940
I-It was... It was a lie?! How much?!

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.520
Wait! How much of it was a lie?!

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.330
Take up your weapon.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.320
Let me teach you one thing.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:28.120
The three Arteros followers are alive.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.590
The one in black clothes who burned up...

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.470
was your man.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:57.080
Any last words?

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.370
I wanted...

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.120
I wanted to bring peace to the world!

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.320
I wanted to bring peace to the wo—

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.590
Oh, really?

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:26.660
So you can only achieve peace 
by killing my compatriots?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.690
In that case, we will never achieve peace

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.320
until we have eradicated 
every last one of you.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:12.740
Ah, so the force those three 
were in charge of failed?

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:17.320
What fools. They should have 
just come straight home.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.310
Shall we send a rescue team?

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.950
Of course not. There are 
only two survivors, yes?

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.040
I believe that is the prudent choice.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.840
The greater problem is that

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:32.550
the heroes, who should be 
neutral toward humanity,

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:35.230
have become our enemies.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.310
You believe it may become 
necessary to fight the heroes?

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.180
I do.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.380
If Kamilto, the fool that he is,

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:45.000
had only temporarily angered them, 
it would not be an issue,

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:48.540
but we must consider the 
worst-case scenario.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.940
Very well.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:53.610
Then begin researching 
ways to kill the heroes.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.210
Understood.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.290
We don't know what the letter he sent said,

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.850
so there's no way to tell 
if this was a success.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.020
That's true.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.220
I'd say it basically was, though.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.570
We rescued their captives and everything.

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:20.070
Although our actual destination 
is still a ways off...

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:21.770
Huh?

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.690
So about the "goods"...

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.480
There are three things I want to try.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.680
Uh-huh...

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.160
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.010
<i>Iu-san and the rest haven't moved...</i>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.260
Do I have cargo bound for Radodorbo?

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:44.550
No, I'm afraid not. I'm sorry.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.870
I see.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.980
Thank you anyway.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:51.960
Just when we'd finally found a merchant...

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:57.110
I looked around, but didn't see anything 
else that looked like a shop.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:04.080
If we just keep going and end up in 
Radodorbo with no goods, the joke's on us.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:08.170
Actually... maybe not.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.020
Huh?

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:14.570
Makuah-san, there's something 
I'd like to ask you.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:15.930
Yes?

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.640
That's the last one.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.800
Are we really taking those with us?

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.540
They might be the goods we need.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:33.020
Yeah, but... to be honest, I don't want 
to be on the same wagon as them...

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.730
I mean, there's a little 
kid with us, you know?

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:38.500
I don't think it sets a good example...

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.360
You don't need to worry about me.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:43.600
Is there anything I can help you with?

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.850
You only just woke up. Just rest, okay?

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.300
Okay!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.090
So pure!

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:56.270
<i>God, this is scary! The possibilities 
of shota are just too infinite!</i>

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:57.790
<i>Scary!</i>

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:03.820
Uh, yeah... of course...

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:05.570
If you really don't want 
to ride in the wagon,

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:08.100
want to take over driving 
the horses for me?

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.590
What? I can?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:10.280
Huh?!

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:11.250
Huh?

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.250
Oh, um... n-nothing.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.190
Please continue.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.890
Wow, really?

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:26.910
Heroes really are amazing!

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.450
I admire you!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.270
And you healed me, too! Thank you so much!

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:36.730
It's okay...

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.040
Is something bothering you?

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.200
Uh, no, nothing.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.480
<i>Damn straight it's bothering me!</i>

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.290
<i>Why did she sigh?!</i>

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.960
<i>Wait, is she...</i>

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.950
<i>actually into him?!</i>

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.620
<i>And she's sad because 
she's not next to him?</i>

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:05.210
<i>Nah, no way. Couldn't be.</i>

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:12.190
Since we're carrying more people now,

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.820
we need to take breaks more often.

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:22.700
Great Hero, um... this may 
not be the time, but...

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:23.490
What?

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:29.490
N-Nothing! Never mind...

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.030
<i>Was she about to confess her love for him?!</i>

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.120
<i>She totally was, wasn't she?!</i>

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:42.440
Oh, yes...

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:47.730
At our current pace, we should reach our 
destination the day after tomorrow.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.010
Got it.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:54.300
Our journey is almost over...

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.920
<i>What's that air of sorrow about her?!</i>

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:03.900
<i>Is she regretting that she'll have 
to part ways with Yotsuya-kun soon?</i>

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:15.640
<i>I guess even someone like Kahvel-san 
gets hesitant about confessing.</i>

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:20.230
<i>Come to think of it, there was 
an event like this in </i>WonSta<i>...</i>

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:26.520
Tsubasa

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:26.520
I love to see you working so hard
for someone else, Onee-sama.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:23.230
When you help a mob character confess,

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:26.260
your affection level with 
Tsubasa-kun shoots up!

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:29.760
Tsubasa-kun! I'll do my very best!

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:33.190
I'm gonna get through this 
event successfully!

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:38.580
Tsubasa-kun... Tsubasa-kyun...

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.510
I wuv you! Oh, God, I told him! Me!

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.410
Um, is she all right?

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:46.090
The lady hero... She's swaying around...

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:47.190
I hope I get to see you 
soon, Tsubasa-kyun...

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:48.040
Uh, yeah... She's fine.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.790
That happens all the time with gamers.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:51.910
Oh...

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.390
I'm getting all riled up...

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:55.520
I can't wait to get back home 
and play games, too...

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:04.010
m 0 0 l 258 0 l 258 200 l 0 200

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:04.010
[Carrier Chicken]

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:04.010
►Omnivorous creatures used to
deliver messages.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:10.310
Switch seats?

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:11.690
Yeah.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:15.940
My butt hurts after sitting 
on that horse for so long.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:27.740
<i>I call it </i>WonSta<i>'s Famous 
"Get the Two Alone" Plan!</i>

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.170
Tsubasa

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.170
Is it all right if I hold you until help comes?

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:34.840
When the two of them are 
alone in a tight space,

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:39.000
it leads to the classic <i>WonSta</i> scene that 
never fails to raise your affection level!

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.940
<i>The two of them alone on a wagon,</i>

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:43.270
<i>the time to say goodbye 
drawing ever nearer...</i>

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:47.850
<i>It all means there's only one thing to do!</i>

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:49.680
You're sleeping?!

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.630
<i>I mean, I know you were up all night,</i>

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:55.010
<i>but don't you have something 
more important to do?!</i>

