00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:14.260
<i>Next is </i>WonSta<i>'s Classic 
"Shared Task" Plan!</i>

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.420
Tsubasa

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.420
You can't cut the pumpkin?
Then let's cut it together.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.560
Trust deepens when two people 
perform a task together!

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.490
One touch makes the heart race!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.300
<i>Yotsuya usually does the cooking alone,</i>

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.510
<i>but just for today, Kahvel-san can...</i>

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.580
Great Hero!

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.920
I found the perfect game!

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.400
We'll have a grand feast tonight!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.960
Whoa, it's huge!

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:42.490
Oh, wow! It's so big!

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:43.040
You've done it again!

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.900
<i>Is that their shared task?</i>

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.980
<i>Where'd those racing hearts go?</i>

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:50.580
Wow! You're so amazing!

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:51.130
You think so?

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.170
Yes, I do!

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.630
But I'm really not...

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:56.160
I wish I could be like you!

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:57.810
Seriously? Aw, thanks.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.030
<i>If orthodox methods don't work...</i>

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.640
Go full yandere!

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:09.710
We don't need to train in the 
middle of the day, do we?

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:15.640
B-But we don't have much time 
left to learn from Kahvel-san!

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:18.130
We'll just do enough to help you digest.

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:19.320
Come!

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:25.140
<i>This is it! The </i>WonSta<i> plan that earned the 
most mixed reviews in the game's history!</i>

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:30.410
Jaga

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:30.410
I'll carve my feelings into you as a scar that'll never fade!

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:35.770
<i>The most controversial method in 
</i>WonSta<i>, used by Jaga-sama...</i>

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:42.040
Kahvel-san can just carve her love into Yotsuya 
to make sure she can leave with no regrets!

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:46.020
<i>There is a form of love that can 
only be expressed through combat!</i>

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:48.010
<i>Kahvel-san...</i>

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:50.940
<i>Yandere was never really my thing,</i>

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:52.530
<i>but this isn't so bad...</i>

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.580
All right, let's switch now.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:55.210
Huh?

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.660
No! This isn't about me!

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:03.990
You were the one who suggested we train!

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.720
No! I don't wanna get cut up!

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:09.190
Just a tiny little slice!

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:09.200
Yotsuya! Why are you just gawking?!

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:14.060
<i>This is not working at all.</i>

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:18.760
Tsubasa-kun, comfort me!

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:20.800
Tsubasa-kun...

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:22.150
Is she really all right?

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:24.390
Uh... I don't know anymore.

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:27.250
<i>I mean, if you set flags on a character,</i>

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.940
<i>you're supposed to have an event 
ready so they can be retrieved!</i>

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:32.730
<i>So why is nothing happening?!</i>

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:36.550
This piece of shit game is so messed up!

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.300
Put more hot guys in it!

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:40.360
Yeah, she must be fine if 
she's able to complain.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:41.190
I want one who'll call me 
"Onee-sama" at a time like this!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.950
Getting mad takes a lot of energy.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:44.770
This game is just shit! Learn from <i>WonSta</i>!

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:50.860
Seriously, Kusue, good job noticing that.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:56.320
There must be delivery companies that 
transport cargo in this world, too.

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:02.630
Yeah, this world made me jump straight 
to the idea of merchants, at first,

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:07.290
but normally, it'd be delivery 
companies that transport cargo.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:13.080
And it was just our luck that they 
have a monthly delivery today.

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:14.680
Here they come!

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.250
And they've got cargo!

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.000
That's gotta be the one!

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:23.320
Cargo bound for Radodorbo?

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.660
Yes, I have some.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.970
Yes!

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:29.600
If you don't mind, please allow 
us to escort you to Radodorbo.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:32.270
Well, I wouldn't mind that...

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:34.600
Now, wait just a minute.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:39.660
Heroes or not, I don't 
need any competition.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:43.000
We can't back down, either. 
Our lives depend on this.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.340
Well, then...

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.270
I have no choice!

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.770
Well? No choice but to do what?

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:13.410
<i>I got myself all exhausted for nothing.</i>

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:17.870
<i>Is Kahvel-san gonna be able 
to retrieve her flags?</i>

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.570
Great Hero...

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:36.180
Do you have a moment?

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:38.230
Uh, sure.

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:48.300
You're not going to sleep?

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.070
I don't need...

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:54.560
No, you're right.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.830
Uh-huh...

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:01.550
Great Hero...

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:05.510
Um, there's... there's...

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:10.820
There's something I've been 
wanting to tell you.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:12.690
Okay...

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:20.060
Thank you.

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:26.630
For helping me avenge Bihmsberg.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.300
I'm deeply, deeply grateful.

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:35.120
Well, I was pissed off at them, too...

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.790
I've wanted to say that all along,

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:45.200
but it was difficult to 
find the right timing.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.590
I feel better.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:50.110
Now I should sleep well tonight.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.180
She's so dutiful.

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:02.350
<i>That was what she wanted to say?!</i>

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.970
<i>Don't be so damn misleading!</i>

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:12.690
You really don't mind carrying 
that stuff in your wagon?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:13.850
Not at all.

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:17.230
We'll get it there no matter the cost. 
You can rest easy.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:20.240
I can't believe I get 
to travel with heroes!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.380
I'll learn so much from this!

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:24.700
It's scary how much his attitude's changed.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.790
Don't worry about it.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:27.980
Off we go!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.790
Since we'll reach Radodorbo 
before the end of the day,

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:41.380
I'd like to review what we're 
going to do upon arrival.

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:45.360
We've prepared three different cargos.

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:47.010
The first is...

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:49.840
the three condemned convicts.

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:52.940
If we get them to a church 
where they'll be kept safe,

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.970
we might complete the quest.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.780
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.83%)</b>

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.780
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.780
<b>Time remaining: approx. 1 day, 15 hours</b>

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.850
If not, we'll try the second...

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.130
the personal effects of the 
dead kingdom soldiers.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:10.280
If we can sell them or get 
someone to accept them,

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.170
they might be counted as "the goods."

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.250
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.83%)</b>

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.250
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.250
<b>Time remaining: approx. 1 day, 14 hours</b>

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.990
And that leaves our third cargo.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.760
Those, huh?

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:31.670
At this pace, we should get there 
with plenty of time to spare...

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:38.250
But will helping to escort a 
delivery man really be enough?

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:42.670
If it does work, then what did 
we go through all that for?

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:44.460
It just seems too easy.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:52.790
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.83%)</b>

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:52.790
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:52.790
<b>Time remaining: approx. 1 day, 13 hours</b>

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:48.810
And we still have the 
other part of the quest.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:52.780
Considering our pace so far, 
that'll be a close call, too.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.290
It's cleared?!

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.130
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.83%)</b>

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.130
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.130
<b>Time remaining: approx. 1 day, 13 hours</b>

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:02.960
It's cleared!

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.580
So this was it.

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:17.080
To think the Kingdom of Deokk was 
carrying out such atrocities...

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:20.890
If you'd like more evidence 
than what we've given you,

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:25.070
go to the church. 
The victims are being cared for there.

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:27.140
Very well.

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:32.720
We truly thank you for bringing us this 
information and stopping their plans.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:35.830
But even if it serves as evidence...

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.630
You really don't need to bring 
severed heads next time.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:51.060
I never would've thought the kingdom 
soldiers' heads would be the right answer.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:55.710
It may have met the conditions 
to be considered "the goods,"

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:59.390
but in the end, I guess it was 
all up to how the Master felt.

00:20:59.390 --> 00:21:00.550
Hey!

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:05.360
I'm so glad we found you!

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:11.800
In any case, we completed one quest.

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:12.960
Good job!

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:15.740
That just leaves covering more of the map.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:18.640
We have a day and a half left.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:19.700
Then...

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:21.030
Let's split up.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:34.330
Wh-Why... do I feel like I've been 
dumped by a girl I didn't ask out?

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:40.020
<b>Heart-Racing Logout</b>

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.210
To: Yotsuya Yuusuke

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:33.150
Do you... really think we 
should stay like this?

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:34.850
Listen...

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:35.900
Let's split up.

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:37.680
Wait! I never asked you out!

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:39.430
Where are you even filming this?!
